From f180fb2d32c17da6a18614e6126f85040d24e1a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LuneOS <claude.ai@herrie.org>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 13:28:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Let audiod claim the legacy com.palm.audio bus names

palmLegacyManager registers com.palm.audio and org.webosports.service.audio,
but ls-hubd refuses LSRegister for a name the executable's role file does not
list, so the module would come up with neither handle. Add both to
allowedNames, give them outbound permissions covering what the Palm-era UI
reaches (telephony, bluetooth, power, systemservice, keys, the shell), declare
the legacy methods in the api file so callers can be granted them, and ship a
service file per name so ls-hubd knows they resolve to audiod.

These are the same names audio-service claims today, which is why the two
cannot be installed side by side -- packagegroup-luneos-audiod conflicts with
audio-service accordingly.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LuneOS-specific legacy API]
---
 files/sysbus/com.palm.audio.service.in        |   4 +
 files/sysbus/com.webos.service.audio.api.json | 150 +++++++++++++-----
 .../com.webos.service.audio.groups.json       |  22 ++-
 .../com.webos.service.audio.role.json.in      |  66 ++++++--
 .../org.webosports.service.audio.service.in   |   4 +
 5 files changed, 191 insertions(+), 55 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 files/sysbus/com.palm.audio.service.in
 create mode 100644 files/sysbus/org.webosports.service.audio.service.in

